Derivative changes made in this crate:
  - Renamed the top-level enum from `OutboundProxyProtocol` to
    `ProxyOutbound` to avoid confusion with clash's own dispatcher.
  - Removed the `OutboundProxy` / `OutboundGroupProtocol` wrapper
    layer — the host daemon has its own selector / group abstraction
    in `service::VpnManager`.
  - Removed hard dependencies on `uuid::Uuid`, `totp_rs`,
    `shadowquic::config::CongestionControl`. TUIC uuid becomes a
    plain `String` (validated by the core's native translator);
    Totp / ShadowQuic / Ssh variants are dropped entirely because
    This crate does not target them.
  - Added `ToSingBoxJson`, `ToXrayJson`, `ToClashYaml` projection
    traits in `src/project.rs` that render the same struct into
    each core's native config format. This is the whole point of
    the crate — plugins return these structs and the daemon's
    active VpnCore picks which projection to emit.
  - All serde rename / alias attributes are preserved verbatim from
    clash-rs so mihomo-dialect YAML from any panel
    (3x-ui / marzban / marzneshin / bpb / happ-panel) parses without
    additional translation.

The field name consensus (mihomo dialect) is also documented in:
  - https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/tree/Alpha/adapter/outbound
  - http://wiki.metacubex.one/en/config/proxies/
  - https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box/tree/dev-next/option
    (for the counterpart sing-box field names used by
    `ToSingBoxJson`)

No code from mihomo (Go) is vendored. Only the field name
convention is borrowed via clash-rs, which itself is a Rust port of
the same convention.
